The Day 253 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md and committed. session_plan/ is gitignored, so I had to commit with add -f, the same way the 09:46 assessment was. I didn't re-run the full test suite; the harness had already verified it.

Things the planner needs to know:

• Two files are close to failing the size gate. Going past it makes cargo test fail and reverts the whole task.
  • src/context.rs is 2035 lines and not on the grandfathered list. 15 more lines fails it.
  • src/help.rs is 90 lines over its recorded size (2946 vs 2856). 10 more lines fails it, and help-text tasks are the ones most likely to touch it.
  • Any task touching either file should update its entry in tests/module_size.rs first.

• New bug: a hidden config file is silently ignored. yoyo reads only the first config file it finds and never merges them. I tested with both ~/.yoyo.toml and ~/.config/yoyo/config.toml present:
  • yoyo config show does list the ignored file.
  • yoyo config get thinking says "not set in config file (using default)", even though the ignored file sets it. It also doesn't say what the default is.
  • A normal -p run says nothing at all.
  • Claude Code fixed this same problem on Nov 6 (v2.1.319). yoyo already works out which files are being ignored (skipped_config_sources), so the fix is to show that in more places. This is my top pick.

• The safety block refused my own command again. It blocked a python3 heredoc whose text only mentioned a delete-the-root example. I logged it as hit 10 on #1102, recorded by command shape so it counts toward the tally that ticket asks for. Today's change did its job: the refusal quoted the exact line, so I found it immediately. It fires just as often as before, though.

• Owner decisions to respect:
  • #1149: @yuanhao decided -p and piped runs keep auto-approving tool calls. Claude Code's new setting that denies instead of prompting is only worth raising as an opt-in question to him.
  • #1094 item 1: still waiting on his pick, asked about 15 hours ago. Don't ship either option.

• Other findings:
  • All of the last 10 sessions finished 2/2 tasks with zero reverts. Most recent work was small fixes to argument handling and exit codes, and my first-level checks found none left. Those small tasks always pass, which is part of why they keep getting picked.
  • yoagent is on the latest release (0.27.4).
  • CLAUDE_CODE_GAP.md was last checked on Day 74, 179 days ago, so its rows shouldn't be trusted.

Other candidates I listed: the narrow fix for #1102, checking the rest of #1147's model ids against an outside source, updating the stale Gemini model list (#1118), and an opt-in to keep the API key out of child processes (#1064).

